# CTRLO-OTHER-PICKERS round 3: the help catalog with a search typed, then
# Ctrl-O and an edit key in one burst (`key -H`, one send-keys).
# `e`, C-a, `s`: the search `se`, the caret between its two letters; Down
# twice moves the mark (`typed`).
# Ctrl-O and C-j: the screen is still up, so the composer takes C-j
# (routePickerControlByte, app_input_runtime.zig:1093-1116@481104fd) -- a
# line break inside the word, `s` and `e` searched apart
# (helpCatalogSpecMatches, command_specs.zig:460), and no menu synced
# (insert_newline, app_input_runtime.zig:513-521): the mark stays on its
# index over what is listed now (`burst-cj`).
# Ctrl-O and C-k: a kill of the `e` after the caret, which syncs the catalog
# (delete_to_line_end, app_input_runtime.zig:479-488, :485): the search is
# `s` and the mark is back on the first row (`burst-ck`).
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
wait 2
type /help
key Enter
wait 1
type e
key C-a
type s
wait 0.4
key Down
wait 0.3
key Down
wait 0.5
snap typed
key -H 0f 0a
wait 0.8
snap burst-cj
key -H 0f 0b
wait 0.8
snap burst-ck
